      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Mitosis is the process a single cell uses to split and create two genetically identical daughter cells, which is essential for growth and tissue repair. It consists of four main phases—prophase, metaphase, anaphase, and telophase—where chromosomes line up, separate, and the cell eventually divides through cytokinesis. Understanding this cycle helps explain how multicellular organisms stay healthy and how new life originates from a single cell.",
